 its zone, picks material by palette, prints label_text on a wall plaque or above the prop. Removes the hand-coded isClaudeEmbassy block \u2014 F47 becomes data-driven like everyone else.\n\n  STAGE C \u2014 generator. tools/qsb_floor_rooms_seed.py reads floor_card.json (archetype + tour_blurb + team_roster) and writes a minimum-viable rooms/ dir per floor: a reception desk, the archetype's signature prop (trading dais for F41-45, library shelves for F57, kitchen line for F80, etc.), and a kill-switch corner where appropriate. Each floor gets a unique combination, not a template.\n\nReview asks (3 strict bullets back please):\n  (1) Does the layout schema (zone + footprint + height + primary_prop + palette + label_text + glow) cover what you need for F46 and what you'd want for F165 Vision Floor, F49 Studio, F44 Accounts?\n  (2) Is back-porting F47's hand-coded props into render blocks the right STAGE A first move, or do you want STAGE B (renderer) shipped first against placeholder data so we can iterate live?\n  (3) For the generator: should archetype-mapped props come from a python lookup table I write, OR should we have a small qwen call per floor that proposes 3-5 props from the tour_blurb? Latter is slower but more unique.\n\nI'm boss with Ross-override but this is YOUR surface too on the F46/your-team side, so your call matters. 3 strict bullets. Two-attempt limit \u2014 if format slips, I take the call and stamp it."}
