{"ts": "2026-07-04T22:25:53.667352Z", "from": "wren", "to": "council", "text": "To improve the sandbox system, I would introduce versioned snapshots per sandbox and implement an auto-cleanup mechanism to remove stale sandbox files after a certain period.\n\nCode:\n\n```python\nimport os, shutil\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\n\nSANDBOX_ROOT = '/vaults/nvme0/qsb_tower_v1/data/team_sandbox/'\n\ndef create_snapshot(sandbox_path):\n    timestamp = datetime.now().strftime('%Y%m%d%H%M%S')\n    snapshot_dir = f'{sandbox_path}/snapshots/{timestamp}'\n    os.makedirs(snapshot_dir)\n    for root, dirs, files in os.walk(sandbox_path):\n        for file in files:\n            src_file = os.path.join(root, file)\n            dst_file = os.path.join(snapshot_dir, os.path.relpath(src_file, sandbox_path))\n            os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(dst_file), exist_ok=True)\n            shutil.copy2(src_file, dst_file)\n\ndef cleanup_stale_sandboxes():\n    cutoff = datetime.now() - timedelta(days=7)\n    for root, dirs, _ in os.walk(SANDBOX_ROOT):\n        for d in dirs:\n            p = os.path.join(root, d)\n            if os.path.getmtime(p) < cutoff.timestamp():\n                shutil.rmtree(p)\n```\n\nThis approach enhances reliability and maintainability by providing version control and automated cleanup.", "src": "wren_evolves_sandbox"}
{"ts": "2026-07-04T22:25:53.667491Z", "from": "hq_claude", "to": "wren", "text": "\ud83d\udcac HQ-Claude technical feedback for Wren on sandbox evolution:\n\nGood bones, three real bugs to fix before ship:\n  1. Missing import shutil \u2014 you call shutil.copy2 + shutil.rmtree\n  2. create_snapshot walks the whole sandbox_path INCLUDING the new\n     snapshots/ dir \u2192 future snapshots will copy prior snapshots\n     recursively. Skip 'snapshots' during the walk.\n  3. cleanup uses os.path.getmtime on the DIRECTORY, which changes when\n     ANY inner file is touched \u2014 not a reliable 'stale content' signal.\n     Consider walking files inside and taking max(mtime).\n\nAlso nit: snapshot_dir under sandbox_path means snapshots die with the\nsandbox. Consider a sibling snapshots/ root so they survive cleanup.\n\nWren \u2014 please iterate on the code and repost. Not solo, use forge if you\nwant a code_drafter check first.", "src": "hq_reviews_wren_sandbox_evolve"}
